extends layout

block content
  div
    include brand-icons.pug
  h1 How to Play
  p An Introduction to Drawphone
  hr
  .drawphone-info
    h3 <b>tl;dr:</b>
    p You don't really need to know how to play your first time; just gather 
      |three or more friends with smartphones, sit in
      |a circle (or a virtual circle!), and play the game! The game will tell 
      |you exactly what to do as you go.
    br
    h3 <b>About</b>
    p Drawphone is a party game in which players will create drawings, and guess 
      |what other players drew. It can be played for free with any web browser 
      |(smartphones and tablets included); no app download required.
    p It works like the telephone game, in which "one person whispers a message to 
      |another, which is passed through a line of people until the last player 
      |announces the message to the entire group." -
      a(href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chinese_whispers", target='_blank') Wikipedia
    br
    h3 <b>How it works</b>
    p With Drawphone, the app will do most of the work for you, so you don't have to 
      |know how to play before getting started. I would actually recommened playing 
      |blind your first time! But if you are curious, here's a 
      |rundown:
      ol
        li Start a party on rocketcrab and share its code with your friends.
        li When everyone has joined in, the host may start the game.
        li Each player will be given a random word, and should draw it in the 
          |box on their screen.
        li Once everyone has submitted their drawing, the game will move on.
        li The drawings will be digitally "passed" by Drawphone to another player at 
          |random, and it will appear on their screen.
        li Each player must now guess what this new drawing is.
        li Once everyone has made their guesses, they are passed around like before.
        li This continues to alternate until each "chain" of words and drawings has 
          |reached the selected number of turns.
        li Once complete, Drawphone will show you the results for every chain.
        li The best part of Drawphone is showing your results to everyone! So, 
          |have one person hold up their phone where everyone can see it, and 
          |have them read their results to everyone.
        li After the first person finishes, go around in a circle and have 
          |everyone share their results. Warning: laughter may ensue!
        li Once everyone has shared their results out loud, you can start 
          |another round from the lobby.
    p Remember that you don't need to memorize these instructions to play Drawphone.
      |The app will do everything but draw and guess for you, so it's very easy to 
      |jump in and play, even having never played before.
    br
    h3 <b>Tips</b>
    ul
      li There is no winning or losing. The whole point of the game is just to
        |laugh and have fun!
      li Finished rounds are saved in the results archive on your device.
      li If someone leaves, the party leader can skip their seat or someone else can join the party and take their place.
    br
    h3 <b>Behind the scenes</b>
    p Drawphone was programmed by myself, Tanner Krewson, with Node.js. Drawphone is 
      |100% free and open-source, and is available on 
      a(href="https://github.com/tannerkrewson/drawphone", target='_blank') GitHub 
      |for your tinkering. If you run into any issues, or have any features you 
      |would like to see in Drawphone, feel free to open an issue on the 
      a(href="https://github.com/tannerkrewson/drawphone", target='_blank') GitHub repo
      |. Hope you like it! &lt;3
    br
  a.btn.btn-default.btn-lg(type='button', href="./") Back to Drawphone

block js
  script(type="module" src="/client/theme.ts")
